@startuml
title Moving tokens while the protocol is paused - what the pause does and does not stop

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam activityBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activityDiamondBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

start
:A power user holding can_pause sets
PauseTransfers { transfers_paused: True };<<#EEF5FF>>
note right
  That transaction may not move the security
  token itself: no_security_token_spent closes
  the pause-and-transfer bypass, where an actor
  would pause and move value atomically under
  the rules that held a moment before.
end note

:transfers_paused == True in the
NFT-authenticated GlobalState datum;<<#EEF5FF>>

if (Does the operation SPEND a programmable-base
UTxO carrying the security token?) then (no - a fresh mint)
  :Only the minting proxy and authority run.
  verify_mint_or_burn reads deactivated,
  never transfers_paused;<<#EEF5FF>>
  :ALLOWED - by explicit decision
  power user can_mint, cap still enforced;<<#EAF6F0>>
  note right
    Pinned by the test
    mint_succeeds_while_transfers_are_paused_by_design.
    Accepted consequence: a holder minted to
    mid-pause cannot move the tokens until
    the pause is lifted.
  end note
  stop
else (yes)
  :The CIP-113 base layer must dispatch
  the spend to a transfer-logic script;<<#EEF5FF>>

  if (Which path?) then ([TransferAct] ordinary transfer, or a standard burn)
    :transfer_logic_validator runs
    over the spent UTxO;<<#EEF5FF>>
    :REJECTED
    transfers_paused == False is a required
    conjunct; no denylist or KYC proof
    compensates for it;<<#FDEEEE>>
    note right
      This is also why a STANDARD BURN is
      blocked while paused, even though the
      burn path itself never reads the flag:
      a burn is a spend, so it re-enters
      this same paused transfer logic.
    end note
    stop
  else ([ThirdPartyAct] seizure, by can_force_transfer)
    :third_party_transfer_logic_validator runs.
    No pause gate, and no source-side checks;<<#EEF5FF>>
    :ALLOWED
    destinations still vetted; at least one
    spent input must carry the token;<<#EAF6F0>>
    note right
      Enforcement stays available during a pause
      by design. Pair it with a negative mint and
      can_burn to retire a position mid-pause.
    end note
    stop
  endif
endif

@enduml
